  // Realms and cultures (CAMPAIGN_OVERHAUL.md 4.1). A realm's culture decides what its villages raise and which lines its lords
  // promote along; "lines" are the troop each role fields at tiers I-VII (each entry must be an upgrade of the one before, or
  // the same troop). Troops carry their culture in troops.json; "common" troops are open to every culture.
  // A realm's "home" is where its land grows from on a new map ([x, z] from -1 to 1; -1 z is the north) and "reach" lets
  // it grow further (map units on the original map) before its neighbours stop it (docs/archive/WORLD.md W1). "relations" are the
  // wars and truces a new campaign opens with. A realm's temper (docs/archive/WORLD.md W5) multiplies the shared rules (1 = as before):
  // "aggression" (wars declared, lords marching for the front), "garrison" (how full its seats are kept), "siege" (how readily its
  // lords lay siege), "tribute" (how soon it takes terms); "hunts": "monsters" sends its lords after goblins, beasts and the dead
  // first. Realms not listed in "relations" start at peace. A culture's "kin" are the cultures whose troops its men may also
  // train as (docs/archive/WORLD.md W3); since W4 every realm's four lines are its own culture's troops.
